111
00:27:52,820 --> 00:27:54,760
that they should repent or they'll be destroyed.

112
00:27:54,760 --> 00:27:57,440
He'd rather they were destroyed, so he doesn't want to deliver the message.

113
00:27:57,440 --> 00:28:00,220
So he runs the other direction, gets on a boat.

114
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:02,080
God sends a storm.

115
00:28:02,080 --> 00:28:08,220
He's eventually overboard in the storm and swallowed by a fish that spits him back up on shore,

116
00:28:08,220 --> 00:28:13,860
at which point, having had an attitude adjustment, he goes to where God has asked him to go and

117
00:28:13,860 --> 00:28:14,640
delivers the message.

118
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:16,420
His enemies do repent.

119
00:28:16,420 --> 00:28:17,220
They are forgiven.

120
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:22,120
And he sits outside the city wishing that they'd been, you know, smitten.

121
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:25,760
So that's a unique story.

122
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:30,520
And it's presented in four scenes.

123
00:28:30,520 --> 00:28:31,920
I just told you a lot of action.

124
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:35,880
But each chapter is kind of a quick scene, the bulk of which is talking, right?

125
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:39,320
And it's a conversation about or to God.

126
00:28:39,320 --> 00:28:42,500
And so the story is really about those conversations.

127
00:28:42,500 --> 00:28:46,860
In the first chapter, which we're going to look at today in addition to introducing the book,

128
00:28:47,360 --> 00:28:48,420
is a sermon.

129
00:28:48,420 --> 00:28:51,200
While he's in the storm, he talks to the sailors about who God is.

130
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,260
And that's really the core of that story.

131
00:28:53,260 --> 00:28:57,600
In the second chapter, he says a prayer from inside the belly of the fish.

132
00:28:57,600 --> 00:29:02,660
In the third chapter, he finally delivers the message of who God is to his enemies.

133
00:29:02,660 --> 00:29:06,380
And in the fourth chapter, he sits outside the city and talks to God about what's happened.

134
00:29:06,380 --> 00:29:09,540
So it's those conversations, four scenes, four conversations.

135
00:29:09,540 --> 00:29:11,900
That really is what this book is about.

136
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:16,720
It's just a rich, compact, and really carefully crafted story,

137
00:29:17,020 --> 00:29:22,120
where God reveals his character in stark juxtaposition to a man's character,

138
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:23,640
a man, unfortunately, like ourselves.

139
00:29:23,640 --> 00:29:29,480
And it shows us who God is and what we look like standing before him.

140
00:29:31,660 --> 00:29:35,140
Which means this is not about a whale, right?

141
00:29:35,140 --> 00:29:39,320
It's not a story about a whale.

142
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:40,460
It's a short book.

143
00:29:40,460 --> 00:29:41,900
It's 47 verses.

144
00:29:41,900 --> 00:29:50,660
Three of them mention the fish, which means about 6%, which means 94% of the story, not about fish, okay?

145
00:29:51,220 --> 00:29:57,400
So, and also, just for the record, this was not a time when this was written.

146
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:59,920
There was not in-depth scientific taxonomy.

147
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:03,720
There were basically two things in the ocean, things you could eat and things that could eat you.

148
00:30:04,260 --> 00:30:06,820
And this was of the second category, right?

149
00:30:06,820 --> 00:30:10,580
In some older translations, it says a sea monster came up.

150
00:30:10,580 --> 00:30:14,940
In some translations, it says a whale because they figured it had to be a whale at some point.

151
00:30:14,940 --> 00:30:17,000
