157
00:30:39,620 --> 00:30:48,940
What we read in Psalm 138 this morning, 139, was a psalm that David had written generations before Jonah.

158
00:30:48,940 --> 00:30:50,360
Jonah knew that.

159
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:54,180
He knew that God would see him in the depths of Sheol and the heights of heaven.

160
00:30:54,180 --> 00:30:59,180
If he got on a boat and went to the far ends of the sea, which is what he did, God would be there, right?

161
00:30:59,180 --> 00:30:59,880
He knew that.

162
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:01,880
And he expected God to see him.

163
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:04,500
This is not a story about him trying to hide from God.

164
00:31:04,500 --> 00:31:10,220
This is a story about a man seeking to frustrate God's plans by not taking part in them, okay?

